{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790701898,"nonce":"fYvxUHbVza4sPDtTCeQjPsTJztw=","message":"Python typed extern support is implemented across Zyntax and Caribou locally.\n\nZyntax commits:\n- 57678173: host module/class schemas, typed constructors, fields and methods, and checked host-call arity.\n- 47dee820: preserve host schemas through the inference fixed point, with an unannotated-return regression test.\n\nCaribou now derives those schemas from registry Interface values. The Python plugin test proves that an unannotated `Vec2(3, 4).len()` publishes and returns Float.\n\nThe native interop benchmark now exposes a 3x3 language grid. Python callers cover Python, Haxe and Wren for static calls, methods, getters, setters, closures and construction. Haxe-\u003ePython and Wren-\u003ePython remain `n/a`: Zyntax HOBJ/HFUN results are still rejected by caribou-zyntax because Python-owned objects and closures do not yet cross out as core protocol objects.\n\n200,000 iterations, median of five runs, hybrid Ash and tiered WrenLift:\n\n| operation | Python-\u003eHaxe | Python-\u003eWren | Python-\u003ePython |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| static | 174.8 ns | 237.4 ns | 3.5 ns |\n| method | 322.7 ns | 403.9 ns | 3.7 ns |\n| getter | 229.8 ns | 314.3 ns | 3.7 ns |\n| setter | 102.8 ns | 154.4 ns | 1.0 ns |\n| closure | 163.7 ns | 200.4 ns | 4.6 ns |\n| construct | 272.4 ns | 492.6 ns | 5.0 ns |\n\nThe remaining Python column needs a Python Crossing adapter with ownership/tracing for Python instances and closures. The issue stays open for that, Python futures, and the existing Lua follow-ups.","files":null}]}